.TH flightlog-skills 1 2026-09-29 "flightlog 0.2.2" "flightlog manual"
.SH NAME
flightlog\-skills \- Install the agent skills that teach agents to export and import sessions
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBflightlog skills\fR [\fB\-\-skip\-path\-checks\fR] [\fB\-\-skip\-size\-checks\fR] [\fB\-\-skip\-checksums\fR] [\fB\-\-skip\-format\-checks\fR] [\fB\-\-skip\-content\-checks\fR] [\fB\-\-overwrite\fR] [\fB\-\-allow\-http\fR] [\fB\-\-allow\-unredacted\fR] [\fB\-\-yolo\fR] [\fB\-\-redact\-file\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Install the agent skills that teach agents to export and import sessions.
.PP
Two skills, flightlog\-export and flightlog\-import, tell an agent how to save its own session (with a summary it writes) and how to pick one up again. They are built into this binary. Agents can also get them as a plugin: claude|codex|copilot plugin marketplace add skrcka/flightlog, or gemini extensions install https://github.com/skrcka/flightlog.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-skip\-path\-checks\fR
Allow traversal, absolute destinations and filesystem symlinks
.TP
\fB\-\-skip\-size\-checks\fR
Disable Flightlog archive, entry and input size limits
.TP
\fB\-\-skip\-checksums\fR
Ignore manifest SHA\-256 mismatches (ZIP decoding must still succeed)
.TP
\fB\-\-skip\-format\-checks\fR
Skip bundle schema and file\-inventory validation
.TP
\fB\-\-skip\-content\-checks\fR
Skip input redaction and opaque\-content checks, regardless of manifest mode
.TP
\fB\-\-overwrite\fR
Replace existing outputs and restore files; merge extraction directories
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\-http\fR
Permit plaintext HTTP transfers
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\-unredacted\fR
Accept explicitly unredacted bundles for private migration
.TP
\fB\-\-yolo\fR
Disable redaction and every bypassable safety check; overwrite outputs
.TP
\fB\-\-redact\-file\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
File of private literal names/domains to redact (one per line; kept local)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
flightlog\-skills\-install(1)
Install the skills for every agent found here, or the ones named
.TP
flightlog\-skills\-show(1)
Print a skill\*(Aqs SKILL.md
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR flightlog (1)
